course: dictionary
lesson: 11240
title: Words from school
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A worksheet is a sheet of paper with questions, exercises or tasks. You write your answers in the spaces. Teachers use worksheets for maths, spelling, reading and science. «The teacher hands out worksheets at the start of the lesson.» Hands out means gives to each pupil, so a worksheet is something you get to work on.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. «A lost worksheet can be got again from a classmate, the teacher or the school website.» You can lose a sheet of paper and get another copy, so the words around worksheet support the school meaning. Check it: swap in «a lost sheet of questions» and it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Worksheet also has a computer meaning: in a spreadsheet program, a worksheet is one page of rows and columns. The sentence tells you which meaning is used. If the sentence talks about pupils, answers and homework, it is the school meaning.
explain: Phrases help too. Fill in a worksheet, finish your worksheet and a maths worksheet all mean working on the paper. «Lucas knows the strict logic; the teacher still hands him a worksheet.» Even a clever pupil gets worksheets, so practice matters for everyone.
fact: A worksheet is a sheet of paper with questions, exercises or tasks that a pupil fills in.
fact: In a computer spreadsheet program, a worksheet is one page of rows and columns.
fact: Phrases with worksheet include fill in a worksheet, hand out worksheets, finish your worksheet and a maths worksheet.
fact: Homework is often a worksheet.
fact: Worksheet is a noun, and its plural is worksheets.
exercise: What is a worksheet? | A book of stories | *A sheet of paper with questions or tasks to fill in | A large map of the school | A pencil case for maths
exercise: «A lost worksheet can be got again from a classmate, the teacher or the school website.» What does this sentence tell you? | Worksheets are never lost | Lost worksheets must be thrown away | Only the teacher has copies | *You can get a new copy if you lose one
exercise: Which phrase means to write the answers in the spaces on the paper? | a computer spreadsheet | throw away your pencil | hand out worksheets | *fill in a worksheet
test: In a computer spreadsheet program, what is a worksheet? | *One page of rows and columns | A sheet of paper for maths homework | A computer game | A kind of pencil
test: In «the teacher still hands him a worksheet», what does still show? | The teacher is angry with Lucas | *Even though Lucas knows the logic, the teacher gives him one anyway | Lucas is hungry and cannot work | The worksheet has already been finished
exam: When a teacher says «Please fill in the worksheet», what does worksheet mean? | A sheet of ice on the playground | A type of school bag | A computer program for doing money sums | *A sheet of questions or tasks to write answers on
